# The rollback runner under cron, for a site that already schedules everything with it (the Windows Task Scheduler takes the
# same command line). `--once` takes at most one approved rollback and exits, so every minute is a fine rhythm: an idle run
# costs one cheap request. Two runs that overlap are safe, the API hands each request to only one of them.
#
# Credentials come from a file only the user can read, not from the crontab.
* * * * * . /etc/lqm-runner.env && /usr/bin/java -jar /opt/lqm/lqm.jar runner --once >> /var/log/lqm-runner.log 2>&1
